1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,860
The habit that changed everything didn't happen in the morning. It happened at the end

2
00:00:04,860 --> 00:00:11,420
of the day. Most people just stop working. They close the laptop and carry all the unfinished

3
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:17,820
work or the threads into dinner, into time with family into sleep. The brain keeps spinning

4
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:22,780
not because something is wrong with you, but because your nervous system doesn't know,

5
00:00:22,780 --> 00:00:30,540
you're done. It's still tracking open loops. My shutdown ritual takes four minutes. I scan

6
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:35,820
what is unfinished, write one line about where I'll pick it up tomorrow. Note one thing,

7
00:00:36,460 --> 00:00:43,020
I actually finished today, and then this is the part that sounds strange. I say out loud,

8
00:00:43,580 --> 00:00:50,540
shut down, complete. That's it. I remember sitting across from my wife at dinner, nodding along to

9
00:00:50,540 --> 00:00:57,180
a story she was telling, and suddenly realizing that I hadn't actually heard the last few minutes.

10
00:00:57,180 --> 00:00:57,200
My body had left the desk, but my mind was still inside a YouTube script, a freelance application,
